      "description": "Fixed 56px bar over a blurred sheet.",
      "html": "<header class=\"ds-header\"><a class=\"ds-brand\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-brand-tile\"><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M11 20A7 7 0 0 1 9.8 6.1C15.5 5 17 4.48 19 2c1 2 2 4.18 2 8 0 5.5-4.78 10-10 10Z\"/><path d=\"M2 21c0-3 1.85-5.36 5.08-6C9.5 14.52 12 13 13 12\"/></svg></span>Remedi</a><nav class=\"ds-nav\"><a href=\"#\">Search</a><a href=\"#\">Interactions</a><a href=\"#\">Pricing</a></nav><button class=\"ds-btn ds-btn-primary\" style=\"height:32px;padding:0 12px;font-size:12px\">Sign in</button></header>",
      "css": ".ds-header{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;height:56px;padding:0 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border,rgba(19,26,21,.1));background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--background,#f6f7f4) 85%,transparent);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);font-family:Manrope,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-brand{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:15px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:var(--foreground,#131a15);text-decoration:none}.ds-brand-tile{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid var(--border,rgba(19,26,21,.1));background:var(--card,#fff);color:var(--primary,#1f6b45)}.ds-nav{display:flex;gap:2px}.ds-nav a{padding:6px 10px;border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;color:var(--muted-foreground,#5c675f);text-decoration:none;transition:background-color .15s,color .15s}.ds-nav a:hover{background:var(--muted,#eef0ec);color:var(--foreground,#131a15)}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Pharmacist's Reference Sheet",
    "overview": "Remedi answers one anxious question: what can I safely take beside this? The page is built to be trusted the way a printed reference is trusted: a cool off-white sheet with a faint dot grid, near-black ink with a green cast, hairline structure, IBM Plex Mono for every label and count, and one botanical green spent on the action, the eyebrow, the leaf mark and the \"this is fine\" signal.\n\nThe tone is calm and slightly clinical rather than wellness-warm. No gradient wash, no glass, almost no shadow; depth is a hairline that firms up on hover. An ochre means the paid tier and the status set carries the safety language; nothing else is coloured.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cool off-white sheet with a 7%-alpha dot grid; near-black ink with a green cast",
      "One botanical green, and it is also the success colour",
      "Hairline borders everywhere; shadows only where a surface actually floats",
      "Manrope for reading, IBM Plex Mono for every label, count and code",
      "Light and dark share every token name; components never branch on theme"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Green Rule",
        "body": "primary is the only accent and it is also success. Do not introduce a second brand hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Alpha Hairline Rule",
        "body": "Borders are ink at 10% alpha, not a solid grey; hover raises them to 18%, never changes their hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ochre Is Money Rule",
        "body": "premium and premium-surface mean the paid plan and never decorate a free surface.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Means Fact Rule",
        "body": "IBM Plex Mono is for labels, counts, prices, codes and reference numbers; sentences are Manrope.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two-Size Body Rule",
        "body": "16px in the hero and search, 14px everywhere else; nothing in between.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline-First Rule",
        "body": "A new card is a 1px border on card. Add .surface-hover if it is a link. No resting shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do set every label, count, price and code in IBM Plex Mono, and every sentence in Manrope.",
      "Do build a new surface as card with a 1px border and no shadow.",
      "Do spend primary on the one action, the eyebrow and the focus ring.",
      "Do make an empty state say why it is empty."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't introduce a second brand hue, or use premium ochre outside the paid tier.",
      "Don't add a resting shadow to a card.",
      "Don't use Tailwind's grey or blue palettes or a literal hex in UI.",
      "Don't animate opacity on above-the-fold content."
    ]
  }
}
